[Event "Sicilian: Najdorf"]

{The Najdorf (5...a6) is the most respected Sicilian. ...a6 stops Nb5 and Bb5, prepares ...e5 or ...e6 and a queenside expansion with ...b5. Black trades a wing pawn for White's d-pawn and gets the half-open c-file.}
1. e4 {White takes the centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... c5 {[%csl Gd4] The Sicilian: fights for d4 from the flank and creates an unbalanced game.}
2. Nf3 {Develops and prepares d4. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
2... d6 {Controls e5 and prepares ...Nf6 without allowing e5.}
3. d4 {Opens the centre. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c5 and controls e5.}
3... cxd4 {[%csl Gc8] Trades a wing pawn for a centre pawn. The c-file opens for Black.}
4. Nxd4 {Recaptures centrally.}
4... Nf6 {[%cal Gf6e4] Hits e4, forcing Nc3 before White can play c4.}
5. Nc3 {Defends e4. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
5... a6 {[%csl Gb5] The Najdorf: covers b5 and prepares ...e5 or ...b5.}
6. Be3 {The English Attack: Be3, f3, Qd2, O-O-O and g4.}
 (6. Bg5 {The old main line, pinning the knight. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
6... e6 {Solid: blunts the pin and keeps d5 covered.}
7. f4 {Prepares e5 or f5. The pawn on f4 controls e5.}
7... Be7 {Breaks the pin.}
8. Qf3 {Supports e4 and prepares O-O-O.}
8... Qc7 {Covers e5 and the c-file. The queen on c7 eyes the knight on c3.}
9. O-O-O {Opposite-side castling: a race begins. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9... Nbd7 {Covers e5 and f6; ...b5 is next. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
)
 (6. Be2 {The quiet Opocensky. The bishop on e2 eyes the pawn on a6.}
6... e5 {[%cal Ge5d4] Kicks the knight and claims d4. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on d4.}
7. Nb3 {Retreats. The knight on b3 controls d4.}
7... Be7 {Develops.}
8. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8... O-O {Castles; Black has a comfortable game. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
)
 (6. Bc4 {The Fischer–Sozin bishop. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on f7 and the pawn on a6 and controls d5.}
6... e6 {Blunts the bishop. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
7. Bb3 {Avoids ...d5 and ...b5 tempos. The bishop on b3 eyes the pawn on e6 and controls d5.}
7... b5 {Gains queenside space.}
8. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8... Be7 {Develops.}
)
6... e5 {[%cal Ge5d4] Kicks the knight and claims space, leaving a backward d6 pawn as the price.}
7. Nb3 {Retreats. The knight on b3 controls d4.}
7... Be6 {[%csl Gd5] Controls d5, the key square. The bishop on e6 eyes the knight on b3 and controls d5.}
8. f3 {Supports e4 and prepares g4.}
8... Be7 {Develops.}
9. Qd2 {Connects for O-O-O. The queen on d2 eyes the pawn on d6 and controls d4 and d5.}
9... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
10. O-O-O {Opposite castling. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
10... Nbd7 {Covers f6 and c5.} *

[Event "Sicilian: Dragon"]

{In the Dragon (5...g6), Black's bishop on g7 is the best piece in the position. White usually attacks on the kingside with the Yugoslav Attack.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... c5 {Sicilian. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
2. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
2... d6 {Prepares ...Nf6. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
3. d4 {Opens. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c5 and controls e5.}
3... cxd4 {Takes.}
4. Nxd4 {Recaptures.}
4... Nf6 {Hits e4. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
5. Nc3 {Defends. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
5... g6 {[%cal Gg6g7] The Dragon: the bishop goes to g7.}
6. Be3 {The Yugoslav Attack.}
6... Bg7 {[%cal Gg7a1] The Dragon bishop rakes the long diagonal.}
7. f3 {Supports e4 and g4.}
7... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8. Qd2 {Prepares Bh6 and O-O-O.}
8... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the knight on d4 and controls e5.}
9. Bc4 {[%cal Gc4f7] Stops ...d5. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
 (9. O-O-O {Allows the central break. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9... d5 {[%cal Gd5e4] The thematic break. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
10. exd5 {Takes. The pawn on d5 eyes the knight on c6.}
10... Nxd5 {Recaptures. The knight on d5 eyes the knight on c3 and the bishop on e3.}
11. Nxc6 {Trades. The knight on c6 eyes the queen on d8 and the pawn on a7 and controls d4 and e5.}
11... bxc6 {Recaptures towards the centre.}
12. Bd4 {Fights the Dragon bishop. The bishop on d4 eyes the pawn on a7 and the bishop on g7 and controls e5.}
)
9... Bd7 {Develops.}
10. O-O-O {Castles long. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
10... Rc8 {[%cal Gc8c3] The c-file.}
11. Bb3 {Removes the bishop from ...Ne5 threats. The bishop on b3 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
11... Ne5 {[%cal Ge5c4] Heads for c4. The knight on e5 eyes the pawn on f3.} *

[Event "Sicilian: Sveshnikov"]

{The Sveshnikov (5...e5) gives up d5 and accepts a backward d-pawn for activity and the bishop pair.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... c5 {Sicilian. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
2. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
2... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
3. d4 {Opens. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c5 and controls e5.}
3... cxd4 {Takes.}
4. Nxd4 {Recaptures. The knight on d4 eyes the knight on c6.}
4... Nf6 {Hits e4. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
5. Nc3 {Defends. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
5... e5 {[%cal Ge5d4] The Sveshnikov: kicks the knight. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on d4.}
6. Ndb5 {Heads for d6 and d5. The knight on b5 eyes the pawn on a7 and controls d4.}
6... d6 {Covers d6.}
7. Bg5 {Pins the defender of d5. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
7... a6 {Kicks the knight. The pawn on a6 eyes the knight on b5.}
8. Na3 {Retreats.}
8... b5 {[%cal Gb5b4] Cuts off the a3 knight.}
9. Bxf6 {Removes the defender. The bishop on f6 eyes the queen on d8 and the pawn on g7.}
 (9. Nd5 {Occupies d5. The knight on d5 eyes the knight on f6.}
9... Be7 {Develops.}
10. Bxf6 {Trades. The bishop on f6 eyes the bishop on e7 and the pawn on g7.}
10... Bxf6 {Recaptures with the bishop pair.}
11. c3 {Brings the a3 knight back. The pawn on c3 controls d4.}
)
9... gxf6 {Recaptures with doubled pawns but the bishop pair.}
10. Nd5 {Occupies d5. The knight on d5 eyes the pawn on f6.}
10... f5 {[%cal Gf5e4] Hits e4 at once. The pawn on f5 eyes the pawn on e4.} *

[Event "Sicilian: Accelerated Dragon"]

{The Accelerated Dragon (4...g6) skips ...d6 to keep ...d5 in one move.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... c5 {Sicilian. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
2. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
2... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
3. d4 {Opens. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c5 and controls e5.}
3... cxd4 {Takes.}
4. Nxd4 {Recaptures. The knight on d4 eyes the knight on c6.}
4... g6 {The Accelerated Dragon.}
5. c4 {The Maroczy Bind. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
 (5. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
5... Bg7 {Develops. The bishop on g7 eyes the knight on d4 and controls e5.}
6. Be3 {Develops.}
6... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
7. Bc4 {Aims at f7. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
7... Qa5 {Pins the c3 knight. The queen on a5 eyes the knight on c3 and the pawn on a2 and controls d5 and e5.}
8. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9. Bb3 {Retreats. The bishop on b3 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
9... d6 {Solid. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
)
5... Bg7 {Develops. The bishop on g7 eyes the knight on d4 and controls e5.}
6. Be3 {Develops.}
6... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
7. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
7... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8. Be2 {Develops.}
8... d6 {Solid. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
9. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9... Bd7 {Develops.} *

[Event "Sicilian: Anti-Sicilians"]

{2.c3 and 3.Bb5+.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... c5 {Sicilian. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
2. c3 {The Alapin. The pawn on c3 controls d4.}
 (2. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
2... d6 {Najdorf move order. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
3. Bb5+ {The Moscow. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
3... Bd7 {Blocks. The bishop on d7 eyes the bishop on b5.}
4. Bxd7+ {Trades. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
4... Qxd7 {Recaptures.}
5. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
5... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
6. c3 {Prepares d4. The pawn on c3 controls d4.}
6... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
7. Re1 {Supports e4.}
)
2... Nf6 {[%cal Gf6e4] Hits e4. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
3. e5 {Kicks the knight. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on f6.}
3... Nd5 {Central knight. The knight on d5 eyes the pawn on c3.}
4. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c5.}
4... cxd4 {Takes. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c3.}
5. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on d4.}
5... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on e5.}
6. cxd4 {Recaptures.}
6... d6 {Challenges e5. The pawn on d6 eyes the pawn on e5.} *
